  "pinned_at_note": "Protected-test race repair candidate. The pin records the exact test-only source identity before this deliberate baseline advance; it does not claim release readiness, production reliability, elapsed soak, live-provider success, host-loss recovery, blank-environment qualification, or research evidence.",
  "justification": "This focused change advances exactly one protected test blob: tests/test_factory_m4_safety.py. The process-group termination assertion previously checked /proc/<pid>/status existence and then opened it, allowing the expected child exit between those operations to raise ProcessLookupError and spuriously fail qualification. The repair performs one status read and treats only FileNotFoundError or ProcessLookupError as the successful disappeared-process outcome; a readable non-zombie child still must disappear within the same bounded polling window or the test fails. Runtime code, trust-boundary semantics, capability probes, UNKNOWN/BLOCKED handling, zero-skip qualification, and every other protected blob remain unchanged. Fresh exact-head protected-owner, capable-runner, and repository qualification are required.",
